# Line endings for this repository.
#
# The batch files under src/runtime/ and src/ci/ are executed by cmd.exe
# inside WinPE. cmd.exe needs CRLF: with bare LF it silently mis-parses
# labels and multi-line blocks. The repo has been bitten by this before,
# so the rule is pinned here instead of relying on core.autocrlf, which
# only applies on Windows checkouts and silently produces LF elsewhere.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Registry scripts are UTF-16LE with a BOM (reg.exe requires the BOM) and
# are handled as binary so git never touches their bytes or line endings.
*.reg binary

# The UWP filelists are read line by line by Wb2List.ps1. LF is fine for
# them, but CRLF keeps the files consistent with the rest of the tree.
src/uwp/filelists/*.txt text eol=crlf
src/uwp/reg/copy/*.txt text eol=crlf
